			     Installation

To install S3Tris, copy S3Tris.app it to any directory (like \APP\) and
install it <Psion-I> from the system screen.  Alternatively, rename it
S3Tris.img, and copy it to the \IMG\ directory, or any other directory
(such as a games alias) referenced by an alias of RunImg.

It was written with the SIBO 'C' SDK, and was written primarily as a
replacement for an OPL version which I wrote last year before I had the
SIBO SDK.


			       Credits

This version was developed from a literal translation of an OPL version
which I wrote around Christmas 1992.  This was rewritten several times
in OPL and then in C before being playable, so I have rechristened this
version 1.0a - all other OPL versions are obsolete (too slow mainly due
to OPL function call overheads and integer arithmetic).  It took
CONSIDERABLE debugging (should have written it in C to start with), so
if you want to send me money, fine.

It could be a good example of creeping featurism, as the options are
now massive.  This does however cater for most people's tastes.  I
think it's better than the Psion version (Tetris on CIS) - it doesn't
crash after 50 lines (panic 73, ha!), and also than Tetrion (Yellow
Computing, FTP'ed from somewhere) - which will only run from an SSD,
and which isn't free.  I also prefer it to Quadris, although that
version has its own merits.

Version 1.1a now utilizes a resource file for all language dependent
strings - this should reduce the amount of memory required during a
run, while also allowing easy translation to other languages.  This
was added when the Help was changed to use the HWIF hHelpSubSystem
call.


				Rules

*Everything* is configurable.  See the built-in help.  Scores are
saved in M:\APP\TMP\S3TRIS.TOP, the default config is saved in
M:\APP\TMP\S3TRIS.CFG.


			      Compiling

S3Tris was written completely with PLIB, HWIF, and WLIB functions, and
as such is not portable (even to other SIBO machines, unless you want
to rewrite all the HWIF sections) in any way.  See the src.zip archive
for all files necessary to recompile.  It also requires the utils.lib,
of which the source code is included.


			      Revisions

1.0a: Initial C release

1.1a:   Modified to utilize resource file - additional optimization

